# Files excluded from the Vercel deployment (kept in the repo).
#
# Local/private build inputs. Vercel CLI reads this file independently of
# .gitignore. Keep credentials and hydrated private-store data out of the
# uploaded source as well as the explicitly staged public/ serving directory.
/data/
/public/
/r2.env
*.env
.env*
/ai-health.json
/.codex/
/AGENTS.md
*.log
#
# Build/scanner sources, documentation, and repository metadata are not runtime
# inputs. Keep only the small script that stages the committed browser assets.
/scripts/*
!/scripts/prepare-vercel.mjs
/docs/
/.github/
/supabase/
/*.md
/.gitignore
#
# Dormant portfolio stack (#269): the Portfolio tab was removed from the site,
# so these endpoints are unreachable (gated/503) anyway. Excluding them from the
# deploy keeps the project under Vercel Hobby's 12-serverless-function limit so
# the live data endpoints + the Discord-gate functions fit. They stay tracked in
# git — to re-enable the portfolio backend, delete these lines (and re-add their
# vercel.json `functions` entries if you want custom maxDuration).
api/config.js
api/portfolio-review.js
api/close-position.js
api/delete-trade.js
